WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.120
Welcome.

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.960
So here we are at step six.

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.040
We're going to connect Continuum to whichever tool

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.120
you're using, so your AI can actually read

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.640
its memory all on its own.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.720
Now, connecting here simply means we're giving

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.560
the tool directions to your memory folder.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.920
We're not making a separate copy

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.680
of it, just pointing the way.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.760
Now, if you're using a local tool, something like

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.800
Codex or Claude Code, the setup assistant is going

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.780
to place two small pointer files Basically, they just

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.180
tell the tool exactly where your memory lives.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.860
After that, it double checks to make sure

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.260
the tool can actually find your context there.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.860
I do want to mention one honest

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.300
limit to keep in mind, though.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.620
Having these files in one project doesn't

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.580
automatically make every app everywhere use them.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.700
You're really just connecting exactly what you plan to use.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.300
A web project, on the other

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.820
hand, works a bit differently.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.460
With the portable option, you get your constitution as

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.020
one single document, which you can then just add

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.980
straight to a chat GPT or CLOD project.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.870
Once you do that, Every single chat

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.870
within that project will start with it.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.790
Just know that while the web chat has

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.270
your constitution, it won't have a live search

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:02.870
of your history back on your Mac.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.270
And whenever your constitution changes, you

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.590
just manually add the new version.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:10.550
Okay, so once it's all connected, starting from your

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.790
very next session, your AI is going to read

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:15.110
your constitution right at the start of the conversation.

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:16.630
And it only does this once.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:18.550
Later on, if it needs more context,

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.150
it'll just look up the findings behind

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.070
it or search through your past conversations.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.390
You don't even have to ask it to do this.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.550
But remember, and this is important to keep

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.870
in mind, whatever the AI reads is going

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.870
to be shared with that AI service.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.550
It works exactly the same as anything

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.550
else you'd paste into a chat box.

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.710
Connect this tool both local tools

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:38.230
or make a portable copy.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.510
It's completely up to you.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.430
You can always start with one method right now

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.430
and then just add another one later on.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:46.150
Whenever you're ready, just press a button below.
